      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and the usual maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. A dose this high greatly increases the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1000 mg per dose.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **Another regimen.** If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that the dose was verified.\n\nOnce you tell me the intended dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
